research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-240861-items/ex-ideals-as-submodules-of-the-regular-module.md:56:1.1 The additive group of $R$ is abelian. For $r,s,x,y\in R$, the ring laws give $r(x+y)=rx+ry$, $(r+s)x=rx+sx$, $(rs)x=r(sx)$, and $1_Rx=x$. Thus $r\cdot x:=rx$ makes $R$ a left $R$-module. [L1, L4, given]
